e dog is running outside" because it\'s more similar to the original sentence in terms of the concepts and elements involved.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: Prototype theory in linguistics and cognitive psychology suggests that people categorize concepts based on prototypical instances rather than strict definitions. This theory could be related to the original question because it implies that our understanding of a concept is influenced by our experience with prototypical examples, rather than absolute definitions.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: Prototype theory may be relevant to the original topic.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: Prototype theory is a concept related to the original question.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: Some people have an exceptional memory ability, also known as photographic memory.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: Some people have exceptional memory capabilities, often referred to as eidetic memory.'}], [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Summarize the input sentence while preserving the exact meaning of the sentence. Do not output any additional explanation. Only output the summary.\nSentence: Some people possess an extraordinary memory ability, often re